- Feature list
    Reference
        syntax
        reach
        note
        - Named Column
            syntax: @price
            reach: tables and line values
            note: references are name-only, positional numbers were removed in 1.6; a digits lead names an Example, never a column
        - Cross Cell
            syntax: @price@Alpha
            note: either order works, @price@Alpha or @Alpha@price
        - Cross Table
            syntax: @Sales Ledger@total@Alpha
            note: name the other table first, the Concept, Example or Attribute it sits under; it may live in any file in the repo
        - Cross Concept
            syntax: @Integer@35@is prime
            note: a Concept written line form is referenced like a table; its Examples are the rows, its attributes the columns
        - Concept Own Value
            syntax: @Measurement@alias
            note: no Example named reads the value the Concept states on its own line, the default its Examples inherit; only a Concept has one, a table is rows and nothing else
        - Past A Local Name
            syntax: @Person@alias@Socrates
            note: the local reading is tried first; a Concept gets its turn when that reading cannot be completed, so an owner's own person attribute no longer swallows the lead
    Constraint
        - Comparison Bound
            keyword: >= > < <= ==
            example: age >=0
        - Listed Value
            keyword: or
            example: 0 =or(0>=1,1==0)
    String Function
        - upper
            turns: widget into WIDGET
        - lower
            turns: WIDGET into widget
        - trim
            turns: padded text into a tight one
        - concat
            turns: three pieces into one
        - split
            turns: a packed value into its fields
        - find
            turns: a part into its position, or zero when it is absent
    Logical Operator
        - and
            true when: every argument is true
        - or
            true when: any argument is true
        - not
            true when: its argument is false
        - xor
            true when: an odd number of arguments are true
    Escape
        - Literal Equals
            escapes: the equals sign
            written: a \= b
            reads as: a \= b

- Working Demonstration
    Sales Ledger|price        |qty >=1|total
    Alpha       |10           |2      |20 =@price*@qty
    Beta        |2 =@Alpha@qty|4      |5
    Total       |             |       |25 =sum(@total)
    
    Ledger Check|from the ledger
    alpha total |20 =@Sales Ledger@total@Alpha
    price sum   |12 =sum(@Sales Ledger@price)

    Person Record
        age >=0
        birth date
        - Ada Lovelace
            age: 36
            birth date: 1815-12-10
        - Alan Turing
            age: 41
            birth date: 1912-06-23
    Label Builder
        - Widget Label
            base: widget
            code: WIDGET =upper(@base)
        - Gadget Label
            base: gadget
            code: GADGET =upper(@base)
